  "term": "Sexual Harassment",
  "definition": "Sexual harassment is a form of discrimination marked by unwanted sexual behavior, such as unwelcome advances, comments, touching, or questions about marital status or sex practices. Although workplace law addresses it in employment settings, it can also occur in schools, athletics, and other social environments, and both men and women may be victims or aggressors.",
